{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqenr7fsfkq","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"handoff e2e claim uses non metric task to avoid metric branch arm","summary":"The /overlay/status in_progress claim for a task carrying a metric spec is refused unless git.currentBranch of the claim workspace is on orch/attempt/*. But the self-register-on-claim hasWorktree check reads overlay.git on the MAIN repo, and targetOverlay does NOT canonicalize a worktree path back to its parent repo (it loads a fresh empty overlay for the literal path). So a metric task cannot satisfy BOTH the worktree-registration check (needs main workspace) and the attempt-branch check (needs worktree workspace) in the sandbox. The T4 e2e (test/handoff-roundtrip.test.js) therefore runs the live claim/self-register/commit leg on a NON-metric task, and covers the metric half (measure + schema metric-conditional + terminal handoff gate) separately on a metric task whose gate does not depend on the claim workspace. Separately: scripts/run-tests.js shows 14 pre-existing FAILs on the clean base (incl. metric-branch-claim, agent-tool-spawn-register, endpoints, sweep, touch-agent) unrelated to T4 — these are the dormant daemon issues from the audit-sprint memory, not introduced here.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T03:32:57.832Z","vec":[-0.02937254123389721,-0.012557702139019966,0.06508106738328934,-0.01855064369738102,0.0540509857237339,-0.06493387371301651,-0.014591081067919731,0.07022497802972794,0.05726756155490875,0.03830231726169586,0.013018550351262093,-0.03700152784585953,-0.03270566090941429,0.05140158534049988,0.052593354135751724,-0.034473199397325516,0.08768809586763382,-0.058780547231435776,0.02603437937796116,0.015436152927577496,0.06340198963880539,-0.03900846466422081,0.04269993677735329,0.003904277691617608,-0.01571313664317131,-0.09710853546857834,-0.09758211672306061,0.007957442663609982,-0.0208146870136261,-0.04415901005268097,0.06114467605948448,0.07781922072172165,